      "summary": "The new RELEASE-ID-06 test is present and checks direct references, but its block regex can stop before the end of an assignment and miss indirect principal or scope expressions.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "minor",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/ReleaseIdentityContractTests.cs",
          "line": 8,
          "message": "The role-assignment regex truncates blocks at the first closing brace, so attributes after a nested block are not checked. Parse balanced blocks or otherwise ensure the test examines the full assignment body.",
          "confidence": 0.76,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RoleAssignmentBlock captures a role assignment body only until the first line containing a closing brace. With a nested block inside the assignment, that closing brace ends the match before later attributes are checked.",
            "failureScenario": "If a valid role assignment has a nested timeouts block before its scope and principal_id, the test omits those attributes. An indirect scope or principal after the nested block can therefore evade the RELEASE-ID-06 direct-reference check."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
